WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.319
Lots of tools detect
problems: posture engines,

2
00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:07.175
scanners, entitlement tools,
certificate inventories.

3
00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:08.500
The rule is simple.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.608
Each one is a detection engine
feeding the one coordination layer,

5
00:00:12.608 --> 00:00:14.475
never a second queue of its own.

6
00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:19.604
That way an over-privileged role and an open
storage account land in the same place,

7
00:00:19.604 --> 00:00:21.338
under the same five clauses,

8
00:00:21.338 --> 00:00:25.713
and access requests from a governance
front end close the same way too.

9
00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:30.217
Two cautions keep this honest: check
each tool's real platform coverage,

10
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:33.806
since on-premises virtualization
kept coming up as a gap,

11
00:00:33.806 --> 00:00:36.937
and give the alternatives
a fair build-or-buy look.

12
00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:38.740
So where does this pattern break?
